<MarketingLayout
  title="Fleet Management"
  description="Open fleet management interfaces, ready-made integrations, and the native Nexigon experience for Rugix Ctrl."
>
  <h1>Fleet Management</h1>

  <p>
    Once your devices are out in the field, you need a way to manage them
    remotely: deploy software updates, monitor their health, and configure
    them at scale. <em>Fleet management solutions</em> handle this, typically
    through a cloud backend and a device-side agent that communicates with
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>Open Fleet Management Interfaces</h2>
  <p>
    Rugix Ctrl exposes documented, open interfaces for installing system and
    application updates and following their progress. A fleet management agent
    can use these interfaces to deliver an update and trigger its installation,
    while Rugix Ctrl handles the update safely on the device.
  </p>
  <p>
    These interfaces let you integrate Rugix Ctrl with your own backend or a
    fleet management solution of your choice. We also provide ready-made
    integrations and reference implementations for several platforms, so you
    do not need to build that connection from scratch.
  </p>

  <h2>Ready-Made Integrations</h2>
  <p>Rugix Ctrl integrates with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="https://nexigon.cloud">Nexigon</a>:</strong> The
      fleet management platform from the creators of Rugix, offering the most
      native Rugix experience, including first-class support for Rugix Apps.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="https://thin-edge.io/">thin-edge.io</a>:</strong> An
      open-source device agent by{" "}
      <a href="https://cumulocity.com">Cumulocity IoT</a> with official Rugix
      support.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="https://memfault.com/">Memfault</a>:</strong> A fleet
      management solution with a strong focus on observability, supported
      through our reference integration.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="https://mender.io/">Mender</a>:</strong> A fleet
      management platform that can serve as the backend for Rugix Ctrl through
      our reference integration.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can also use Rugix Ctrl without any fleet management solution at all,
    or build your own integration. For technical details on each integration,
    see the{" "}
    <a href="/docs/ctrl/integration/fleet-management/">fleet management documentation</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Why Nexigon?</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://nexigon.cloud">Nexigon</a> is the commercial fleet
    management platform from <a href="https://silitics.com">Silitics</a>, the
    company behind Rugix. Because the two projects are developed side by side,
    Nexigon offers the most native Rugix integration and a polished operator
    experience for managing Rugix-based devices at scale.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Native Rugix Apps management:</strong> Inspect installed apps,
      deploy new versions from a Nexigon repository, follow live logs, and
      start, stop, roll back, or remove apps directly from the Nexigon UI.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Rugix-aware OTA workflows:</strong> Manage update artifacts,
      stage rollouts across the fleet, track progress in real time, and retain
      a complete audit trail.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Secure remote operations:</strong> Access devices remotely,
      inspect their health, and run commands without exposing incoming ports or
      operating a VPN.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can start with a{" "}
    <a href="https://nexigon.cloud">free evaluation</a> and follow the{" "}
    <a href="https://docs.nexigon.dev/rugix/getting-started">getting started guide</a>{" "}
    for using Rugix and Nexigon together.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nexigon's close integration does not change our open-source commitment:
    Rugix remains permissively licensed and contains no Nexigon-specific code,
    and we will not degrade its functionality to steer users toward Nexigon.
    Read our <a href="/open-source-commitment">Commitment to Open Source</a>.
  </p>
</MarketingLayout>
